ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the atmospheric chemical mechanisms governing Photochemical Smog formation, formulating the cyclic reactions of NOx, VOCs, ozone, and PAN.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Atmospheric Reaction Kinetics and Photochemical Smog Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   1. Environmental Initiation \(Primary Pollutants\):) Tj
T*
(   Photochemical smog forms in warm, sunny urban basins with high vehicle emissions of nitric) Tj
T*
(   oxide \(NO\) and unburned Volatile Organic Compounds \(VOCs / reactive hydrocarbons RH\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Fundamental Inorganic Nitrogen Dioxide Photolytic Cycle:) Tj
T*
(   - Early morning traffic emits NO:) Tj
T*
(   NO + 1/2 O2 -> NO2 \(slow thermal oxidation\).) Tj
T*
(   - In the presence of ultraviolet sunlight \(lambda < 420 nm\), NO2 photolyzes:) Tj
T*
(   NO2 + h*nu -> NO + O\(.3P\) \(Atomic oxygen triplet\).) Tj
T*
(   - The reactive atomic oxygen rapidly combines with molecular oxygen in the presence of a) Tj
T*
(   third-body stabilizer \(M = N2 or O2\):) Tj
T*
(   O\(.3P\) + O2 + M -> O3 + M \(Ground-level ozone formation\).) Tj
T*
(   - Under unpolluted conditions, ozone reacts with NO to re-form NO2 in a dynamic photostationary) Tj
T*
(   state:) Tj
T*
(   O3 + NO -> NO2 + O2.) Tj
T*
(   3. The Perturbation by Volatile Organic Compounds \(VOCs\):) Tj
T*
(   Hydrocarbons disrupt this steady state by consuming NO without destroying ozone:) Tj
T*
(   - Hydroxyl radical attack on hydrocarbons:) Tj
T*
(   RH + .OH -> R. + H2O \(Alkyl radical formation\).) Tj
T*
(   - Reaction with atmospheric oxygen:) Tj
T*
(   R. + O2 + M -> RO2. \(Alkylperoxy radical\).) Tj
T*
(   - Oxidation of NO to NO2 by peroxy radicals:) Tj
T*
(   RO2. + NO -> RO. + NO2.) Tj
T*
(   Because RO2. oxidizes NO to NO2 without consuming an ozone molecule, O3 continuously) Tj
T*
(   accumulates to toxic levels \(> 100-200 ppb\)!) Tj
T*
(   4. Synthesis of Peroxyacetyl Nitrate \(PAN\):) Tj
T*
(   Acetaldehyde oxidation forms the acetylperoxy radical, which combines with NO2:) Tj
T*
(   CH3CHO + .OH -> CH3C\(=O\). + H2O) Tj
T*
(   CH3C\(=O\). + O2 -> CH3C\(=O\)OO. \(Acetylperoxy radical\)) Tj
T*
(   CH3C\(=O\)OO. + NO2 <-> CH3C\(=O\)OONO2 \(Peroxyacetyl Nitrate / PAN\).) Tj
T*
(   PAN is a potent lachrymator, eye irritant, foliar phytotoxin, and atmospheric thermal reservoir) Tj
T*
(   for NOx transport.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
