(   [Problem Statement]: Contrast Classical \(London-type\) Smog with Photochemical \(Los Angeles-type\) Smog in terms of chemistry, meteorology, and pathology.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Comparative Analysis: Classical \(London\) Smog vs. Photochemical \(Los Angeles\) Smog:) Tj
T*
(   1. Historical Paradigm:) Tj
T*
(   - London Smog \(December 1952\): A severe sulfurous, reducing smog disaster that killed over) Tj
T*
(   4,000 to 12,000 people in Greater London within five days.) Tj
T*
(   - Los Angeles Smog \(mid-1940s onward\): An oxidizing, photochemical smog associated with dense) Tj
T*
(   automobile emissions in sunny coastal basins.) Tj
T*
(   2. Comparative Evaluation Matrix:) Tj
T*
(   - Parameter: Primary Chemical Character) Tj
T*
(   * London Smog: Chemically REDUCING smog dominated by high concentrations of sulfur dioxide) Tj
T*
(   \(SO2\) and carbonaceous soot particulates.) Tj
T*
ET

