(   CaCO3 \(s\) + H2SO4 \(aq\) + H2O -> CaSO4.2H2O \(s\) \(Gypsum\) + CO2 \(g\)) Tj
T*
(   - Chemical Pathology: Calcium carbonate is converted into calcium sulfate dihydrate \(gypsum\).) Tj
T*
(   - Volume Expansion & Spalling: Gypsum has a molar volume nearly double that of calcite. As) Tj
T*
(   crystals form in micro-fissures, internal crystallographic stress causes the marble surface to) Tj
T*
(   blister, flake, and undergo crumbling \(termed 'Marble Cancer'\), compounded by soot) Tj
T*
(   discoloration.) Tj
