(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate the physical operating principles of an Electrostatic Precipitator \(ESP\), derive the Deutsch-Anderson collection efficiency, and analyze resistivity.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Physics, Operation, and Efficiency Formulation of Electrostatic Precipitators \(ESP\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Operating Principles:) Tj
T*
(   Electrostatic Precipitators are industrial air pollution control systems designed to remove) Tj
T*
(   fine fly ash particulates \(PM2.5 and PM10\) from boiler flue gas streams with efficiencies) Tj
T*
(   exceeding 99.5%.) Tj
T*
(   - Process Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   Consists of grounded, parallel vertical collecting plates \(anodes\) spaced 200 to 400 mm apart,) Tj
T*
(   with high-voltage discharge wires \(cathodes\) suspended centrally between them.) Tj
T*
(   - Negative Corona Generation: A high-voltage negative direct current \(40 to 70 kV DC\) applied) Tj
T*
(   to the discharge wires creates an intense electric field \(> 5 kV/cm\) near the wire tip. This) Tj
T*
(   accelerates free electrons, ionizing flue gas molecules \(O2, CO2, N2\) into a visible electrical) Tj
T*
(   corona.) Tj
T*
(   - Particle Charging: Gas ions collide with ash particles. Particles > 1 micron are charged by) Tj
T*
(   Field Charging \(ion bombardment along field lines\); particles < 0.2 microns are charged by) Tj
T*
(   Diffusion Charging \(Brownian thermal motion\).) Tj
T*
(   - Migration and Precipitation: The electrostatic Coulomb force \(F_e = q * E\) accelerates the) Tj
T*
(   negatively charged particles across the gas stream toward the grounded positive collecting) Tj
T*
(   plates.) Tj
T*
(   - Rapping and Hoppers: Mechanical rapping hammers strike the collecting plates periodically,) Tj
T*
(   causing the agglomerated ash cake to dislodge and slide by gravity into bottom storage hoppers.) Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Derivation of Deutsch-Anderson Efficiency Equation:) Tj
T*
(   - Consider an ESP of total collection plate area A \(m2\) treating gas flow rate Q \(m3/s\).) Tj
T*
(   - Let particle concentration entering a differential plate length be C. In travel time dt, the) Tj
T*
(   fraction of particles reaching the collecting plate across channel spacing is given by:) Tj
T*
(   -dC / C = \(w * dA\) / Q) Tj
T*
(   Where w is the effective particle migration velocity \(m/s\).) Tj
T*
(   - Integrating across the entire ESP from inlet \(C_in\) to outlet \(C_out\):) Tj
T*
(   Integral_{C_in}^{C_out} \(dC / C\) = - \(w / Q\) * Integral_{0}^{A} dA) Tj
T*
(   ln\(C_out / C_in\) = - \(w * A / Q\)) Tj
T*
(   C_out / C_in = exp[ - \(w * A / Q\) ]) Tj
T*
(   - Fractional Collection Efficiency eta:) Tj
T*
(   eta = \(C_in - C_out\) / C_in = 1 - \(C_out / C_in\) = 1 - exp[ - \(w * A / Q\) ]) Tj
T*
(   3. Impact of Fly Ash Electrical Resistivity:) Tj
T*
(   - Optimal ash resistivity is 10^4 to 10^10 Ohm-cm.) Tj
T*
(   - High Resistivity \(> 10^10 Ohm-cm, typical of low-sulfur Indian coals\): The collected ash) Tj
T*
(   layer acts as an electrical insulator. Charge builds up until electrical breakdown occurs) Tj
T*
(   through the ash pores, creating 'Back Corona' that emits positive ions, discharging incoming) Tj
T*
(   particles and destroying collection efficiency.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
