(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the catalytic chemistry of Automotive Three-Way Catalytic Converters, detailing the role of Pt, Pd, Rh, and the closed-loop lambda oxygen sensor.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Automotive Three-Way Catalytic Converters: Catalyst Metallurgy, Stoichiometry, and Closed-Loop) Tj
T*
(   Control:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Three Primary Regulated Pollutants:) Tj
T*
(   Internal combustion gasoline engines emit three hazardous exhaust gases:) Tj
T*
(   - Carbon Monoxide \(CO\): Toxic product of incomplete fuel combustion.) Tj
T*
(   - Unburned Hydrocarbons \(HC / VOCs\): Fuel molecules escaping quench zones.) Tj
T*
(   - Nitrogen Oxides \(NO and NO2, collectively NOx\): Formed by high-temperature thermal fixation) Tj
T*
(   of atmospheric N2 and O2 in the combustion chamber.) Tj
T*
(   2. Catalyst Structure and Active Noble Metals:) Tj
T*
(   - Monolithic Substrate: A ceramic cordierite \(2MgO.2Al2O3.5SiO2\) honeycomb structure extruded) Tj
T*
(   with 400 to 600 micro-channels per square inch to provide massive geometric contact area with) Tj
T*
(   minimal exhaust backpressure.) Tj
T*
(   - Washcoat: A porous gamma-Al2O3 layer containing ceria-zirconia \(CeO2-ZrO2\) as an Oxygen) Tj
T*
(   Storage Component \(OSC\).) Tj
T*
(   - Active Catalyst Loading:) Tj
T*
(   * Platinum \(Pt\) and Palladium \(Pd\): Oxidation catalysts.) Tj
T*
(   * Rhodium \(Rh\): Reduction catalyst.) Tj
T*
(   3. Simultaneous Heterogeneous Catalytic Reactions:) Tj
T*
(   - Reduction Stage \(Catalyzed by Rhodium\):) Tj
T*
(   2 NO + 2 CO --[Rh]--> N2 + 2 CO2) Tj
T*
(   2 NO + 2 H2 --[Rh]--> N2 + 2 H2O) Tj
T*
(   NOx is selectively reduced to harmless diatomic nitrogen \(N2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Oxidation Stage \(Catalyzed by Platinum and Palladium\):) Tj
T*
(   2 CO + O2 --[Pt/Pd]--> 2 CO2) Tj
T*
(   C_x H_y + \(x + y/4\) O2 --[Pt/Pd]--> x CO2 + \(y/2\) H2O) Tj
T*
(   Carbon monoxide and unburned hydrocarbons are fully oxidized to carbon dioxide and water vapor.) Tj
T*
(   4. Closed-Loop Lambda \(lambda\) Oxygen Sensor Feedback:) Tj
T*
(   - High simultaneous conversion \(> 95%\) of ALL THREE pollutants occurs exclusively within an) Tj
T*
(   extremely narrow air-to-fuel ratio window: lambda = 1.000 +/- 0.005 \(Stoichiometric AFR = 14.7) Tj
T*
(   kg air per kg gasoline\).) Tj
T*
(   - If mixture is Lean \(lambda > 1, excess oxygen\): CO and HC are oxidized, but NOx reduction) Tj
T*
(   efficiency plummets.) Tj
T*
(   - If mixture is Rich \(lambda < 1, oxygen deficit\): NOx is reduced, but CO and HC oxidation) Tj
T*
(   collapses.) Tj
T*
(   - The zirconia oxygen sensor \(lambda sensor\) in the exhaust pipe continuously measures residual) Tj
T*
(   O2 partial pressure, feeding real-time millivolt signals to the Engine Control Unit \(ECU\) to) Tj
T*
(   adjust electronic fuel injectors hundreds of times per minute.) Tj
