(   [Problem Statement]: Compare the analytical methodologies and biochemical kinetics of Biochemical Oxygen Demand \(BOD5\) and Chemical Oxygen Demand \(COD\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Comparative Analytical Chemistry and Kinetics: BOD5 versus COD:) Tj
T*
(   1. Fundamental Definitions:) Tj
T*
(   - Biochemical Oxygen Demand \(BOD5\): The mass of molecular dissolved oxygen required by aerobic) Tj
T*
(   heterotrophic microorganisms to biochemically oxidize biodegradable organic matter present in a) Tj
T*
(   unit volume of wastewater during an incubation period of 5 days at 20 deg C in the dark.) Tj
T*
(   - Chemical Oxygen Demand \(COD\): The mass of oxygen equivalent required to chemically oxidize) Tj
T*
(   virtually ALL organic matter \(both biodegradable and non-biodegradable refractory organics\)) Tj
T*
(   using a boiling, acidified strong chemical oxidant \(potassium dichromate\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Analytical Methodologies:) Tj
T*
(   - Standard 5-Day BOD Procedure \(APHA Method 5210B\):) Tj
T*
(   * Wastewater sample is diluted with nutrient-buffered, aerated dilution water \(containing) Tj
T*
(   phosphate buffer, MgSO4, CaCl2, FeCl3, and microbial seed\).) Tj
T*
(   * Incubation in airtight 300 mL glass BOD bottles at 20.0 +/- 1.0 deg C for exactly 5 days.) Tj
T*
(   * Initial DO \(DO_i\) and final 5-day DO \(DO_f\) are determined via the Azide Modification of the) Tj
T*
(   Winkler Titration or membrane electrochemical probes:) Tj
T*
(   BOD5 \(mg/L\) = [ \(DO_i - DO_f\) - \(B_i - B_f\) * \(1 - P\) ] / P) Tj
T*
(   Where P is the decimal volumetric fraction of wastewater sample, and B represents seed blank) Tj
T*
(   values.) Tj
T*
(   - Open Reflux COD Procedure \(APHA Method 5220B\):) Tj
T*
(   * Sample is refluxed for 2.0 hours with an excess of standard potassium dichromate \(0.25 N) Tj
T*
(   K2Cr2O7\) in 50% concentrated sulfuric acid \(H2SO4\) in the presence of silver sulfate \(Ag2SO4,) Tj
T*
(   catalyst for straight-chain aliphatic oxidation\) and mercuric sulfate \(HgSO4, masking agent to) Tj
T*
(   precipitate interfering chloride ions as non-reactive [HgCl4]^2-\).) Tj
T*
(   * Excess unreduced dichromate is back-titrated with standard Ferrous Ammonium Sulfate \(FAS\)) Tj
T*
(   using Ferroin indicator \(sharp color transition from blue-green to reddish-brown\):) Tj
T*
(   COD \(mg/L\) = [ \(A - B\) * M_FAS * 8000 ] / V_sample.) Tj
T*
(   3. The COD/BOD Biodegradability Ratio:) Tj
T*
(   - Domestic Raw Sewage: COD/BOD5 ratio typically 1.5 to 2.0 \(highly biodegradable\).) Tj
T*
ET

