T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the Streeter-Phelps Dissolved Oxygen \(DO\) Sag Equation, and determine the critical oxygen deficit time \(tc\) and location \(xc\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Mathematical Derivation of the Streeter-Phelps Dissolved Oxygen Sag Equation:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Conceptual Model \(Harold Streeter and Earle Phelps, 1925\):) Tj
T*
(   Models the balance between two simultaneous, competing kinetic processes occurring in a river) Tj
T*
(   downstream of an organic wastewater discharge:) Tj
T*
(   - Deoxygenation: Bacterial consumption of dissolved oxygen to oxidize organic matter \(modeled) Tj
T*
(   as a first-order reaction with rate constant k_d, day^-1\).) Tj
T*
(   - Reaeration: Atmospheric physical dissolution of oxygen across the air-water interface driven) Tj
T*
(   by concentration gradients \(first-order rate constant k_r, day^-1\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Differential Formulation:) Tj
T*
(   Define the Dissolved Oxygen Deficit D at time t as:) Tj
T*
(   D\(t\) = DO_saturation - DO\(t\)) Tj
T*
(   The net rate of change of oxygen deficit is:) Tj
T*
(   dD/dt = \(Rate of Deoxygenation\) - \(Rate of Reaeration\) = k_d * L\(t\) - k_r * D) Tj
T*
(   Where L\(t\) is the remaining ultimate carbonaceous BOD at travel time t:) Tj
T*
(   L\(t\) = L_0 * exp\(-k_d * t\), with L_0 being the initial river-waste blend ultimate BOD.) Tj
T*
(   Substitute L\(t\):) Tj
T*
(   dD/dt + k_r * D = k_d * L_0 * exp\(-k_d * t\)) Tj
T*
(   3. Integration via Integrating Factor:) Tj
T*
(   Integrating factor IF = exp\(Integral k_r dt\) = exp\(k_r * t\).) Tj
T*
(   Multiply both sides by exp\(k_r * t\):) Tj
T*
(   d/dt [ D * exp\(k_r * t\) ] = k_d * L_0 * exp[ \(k_r - k_d\) * t ]) Tj
T*
(   Integrating from t = 0 \(where D = D_0, the initial mixed deficit\) to time t:) Tj
T*
(   D\(t\) = [ \(k_d * L_0\) / \(k_r - k_d\) ] * [ exp\(-k_d * t\) - exp\(-k_r * t\) ] + D_0 * exp\(-k_r * t\)) Tj
T*
(   This is the classical Streeter-Phelps Oxygen Sag Equation!) Tj
T*
(   4. Derivation of Critical Time \(t_c\) and Critical Deficit \(D_c\):) Tj
T*
(   The critical point \(lowest DO, maximum deficit\) occurs where dD/dt = 0 \(deoxygenation rate) Tj
T*
(   equals reaeration rate\):) Tj
T*
(   k_d * L_0 * exp\(-k_d * t_c\) = k_r * D_c) Tj
T*
(   Differentiating the equation and setting to zero yields:) Tj
T*
(   t_c = [ 1 / \(k_r - k_d\) ] * ln [ \(k_r / k_d\) * \(1 - D_0 * \(k_r - k_d\) / \(k_d * L_0\)\) ]) Tj
T*
(   The critical downstream distance is: x_c = u * t_c, where u is the mean river flow velocity.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
