T*
(   - Waste Activated Sludge \(WAS\) Line: Discharges excess synthesized microbial biomass to control) Tj
T*
(   sludge age.) Tj
T*
(   2. Microbial Floc Ecology:) Tj
T*
(   The functional unit is the Activated Sludge Floc: an agglomeration of heterotrophic bacteria) Tj
T*
(   \(Zoogloea ramigera, Pseudomonas\), encapsulated within an extracellular polymeric substance) Tj
T*
(   \(EPS\) matrix composed of polysaccharides, proteins, and DNA. Ciliated protozoa \(Vorticella,) Tj
T*
(   Epistylis\) graze on free-swimming dispersed bacteria, clarifying the effluent water.) Tj
T*
(   3. Crucial Engineering Operational Parameters:) Tj
T*
(   - Food-to-Microorganism \(F/M\) Ratio:) Tj
T*
(   Quantifies the organic loading rate per unit of microbial biomass per day:) Tj
T*
(   F/M = \(Q * S_0\) / \(V * X\)) Tj
T*
(   Where Q is influent flow \(m3/day\), S_0 is influent BOD5 \(mg/L\), V is aeration tank volume \(m3\),) Tj
T*
(   and X is MLSS \(mg/L\).) Tj
T*
(   * Standard Conventional ASP operates at F/M = 0.2 to 0.4 day^-1.) Tj
T*
(   * High F/M \(> 0.6\) leads to incomplete BOD removal and turbid effluent.) Tj
T*
(   * Low F/M \(< 0.1, Extended Aeration\) promotes endogenous respiration and highly stable,) Tj
T*
(   well-settling sludge.) Tj
T*
(   - Mean Cell Residence Time \(Sludge Age / Solids Retention Time, theta_c\):) Tj
T*
(   The average time that microbial biomass remains in the system:) Tj
T*
(   theta_c = \(V * X\) / \(Q_w * X_w + Q_e * X_e\)) Tj
T*
(   Where Q_w is waste sludge flow rate, X_w is waste sludge concentration, and Q_e * X_e is) Tj
T*
(   effluent suspended solids loss.) Tj
T*
(   * Conventional ASP maintains theta_c = 5 to 15 days.) Tj
T*
(   * Nitrification requires theta_c > 10 to 12 days to prevent washout of slow-growing autotrophic) Tj
T*
(   nitrifiers \(Nitrosomonas and Nitrobacter\).) Tj
