T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Biochemical Engineering Mechanics of Upflow Anaerobic Sludge Blanket \(UASB\) Reactors:) Tj
T*
(   1. Operational Architecture \(Gatze Lettinga, 1970s\):) Tj
T*
(   The UASB reactor is an advanced high-rate anaerobic wastewater treatment system that treats) Tj
T*
(   high-strength organic industrial effluents \(breweries, distilleries, food processing, dairy\)) Tj
T*
(   without requiring mechanical mixing or artificial immobilization carriers.) Tj
T*
(   - Flow Regime: Wastewater is introduced uniformly at the bottom of the column reactor and flows) Tj
T*
(   vertically upward through a dense bed of highly active anaerobic microbial sludge.) Tj
T*
(   2. Anaerobic Sludge Granulation Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   - Under continuous selective upward hydraulic shear stress \(upflow velocity v_up = 0.5 to 1.5) Tj
T*
(   m/h\), dispersed and poorly settling biomass is washed out, while well-settling microbial) Tj
T*
(   aggregates are retained.) Tj
T*
(   - Granule Structure: Microorganisms self-aggregate into spherical, dense biological granules) Tj
T*
(   \(1.0 to 3.5 mm diameter\) with extraordinary settleability \(sludge volume index SVI < 20 mL/g,) Tj
T*
(   settling velocity 20 to 60 m/h\).) Tj
T*
(   - Layered Microbial Stratification:) Tj
T*
(   * Outer Layer: Acidogenic and hydrogen-producing acetogenic bacteria hydrolyzing incoming) Tj
T*
(   sugars and amino acids.) Tj
T*
(   * Middle Layer: Syntrophic propionate- and butyrate-oxidizing bacteria.) Tj
T*
(   * Inner Core: Densely packed acetoclastic methanogens \(Methanosaeta concilii\) converting) Tj
T*
(   acetate into CH4 and CO2.) Tj
T*
(   3. The Three-Phase Gas-Liquid-Solid \(GLS\) Separator:) Tj
T*
(   Located in the upper section of the UASB reactor, the GLS separator consists of engineered) Tj
