(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the chemical reaction mechanisms of Advanced Oxidation Processes \(AOPs\), focusing on Fenton's Reagent, Photo-Fenton, and Ozone/UV systems.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Advanced Oxidation Processes \(AOPs\): Free Radical Chemistry and Reaction Kinetics:) Tj
T*
(   1. Fundamental Principles of AOPs:) Tj
T*
(   Advanced Oxidation Processes are near-ambient temperature and pressure aqueous water treatment) Tj
T*
(   technologies based on the in-situ generation of unselective, highly reactive Hydroxyl Free) Tj
T*
(   Radicals \(.OH\).) Tj
T*
(   - Thermodynamic Oxidation Power:) Tj
T*
(   * Hydroxyl Radical \(.OH\): Standard reduction potential E0 = +2.80 V \(exceeded only by fluorine) Tj
T*
(   gas, F2 E0 = +3.03 V\).) Tj
T*
(   * In comparison: Ozone \(O3, +2.07 V\), Hydrogen Peroxide \(H2O2, +1.77 V\), Chlorine \(Cl2, +1.36) Tj
T*
(   V\).) Tj
T*
(   - Kinetics: Hydroxyl radicals react with refractory organic compounds at near) Tj
T*
(   diffusion-controlled rate constants \(k = 10^8 to 10^10 M^-1.s^-1\) via hydrogen abstraction,) Tj
T*
(   electrophilic addition to aromatic rings, and electron transfer, mineralizing pollutants into) Tj
T*
(   CO2, H2O, and mineral acids.) Tj
T*
(   2. Classical Fenton's Reagent \(Fe2+ / H2O2\):) Tj
T*
(   - Catalytic Cycle:) Tj
T*
(   Fe2+ + H2O2 -> Fe3+ + .OH + OH- \(Initiation, k = 76 M^-1.s^-1\)) Tj
T*
(   Fe3+ + H2O2 -> Fe2+ + .O2H + H+ \(Rate-limiting reduction, k = 0.01 M^-1.s^-1\).) Tj
T*
(   - Strict pH Window: Optimal reaction occurs strictly at pH 2.8 to 3.2. At pH > 4.0, ferric iron) Tj
T*
(   precipitates irreversibly as ferric hydroxide [Fe\(OH\)3] sludge, halting catalytic turnover.) Tj
T*
(   3. Photo-Fenton System \(Fe2+ / H2O2 / UV-vis\):) Tj
T*
(   Irradiation with ultraviolet or visible light \(lambda < 400 nm\) dramatically accelerates the) Tj
T*
(   process through photochemical reduction of the photoactive ferric complex:) Tj
T*
(   [Fe\(OH\)]^2+ + h*nu -> Fe2+ + .OH) Tj
T*
(   This photoreduction regenerates ferrous catalyst \(Fe2+\) continuously while producing an) Tj
T*
(   additional hydroxyl radical, reducing iron dosage requirements by 90%.) Tj
T*
(   4. Ozone / Ultraviolet \(O3 / UV\) System:) Tj
T*
(   Photolysis of dissolved ozone by shortwave UV radiation \(lambda = 254 nm\) generates hydrogen) Tj
T*
(   peroxide as an intermediate, which photolyzes into hydroxyl radicals:) Tj
T*
(   O3 + H2O + h*nu \(254 nm\) -> H2O2 + O2) Tj
T*
(   H2O2 + h*nu -> 2 .OH.) Tj
T*
