(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the physicochemical weathering of Marine Oil Spills, and evaluate mechanical containment and bioremediation by Alcanivorax borkumensis.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Marine Petroleum Spills: Weathering Dynamics, Mechanical Containment, and Bioremediation:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physicochemical Weathering Processes:) Tj
T*
(   When crude oil discharges into the marine environment \(e.g., Deepwater Horizon, Exxon Valdez\),) Tj
T*
(   the slick undergoes complex physical and chemical transformations:) Tj
T*
(   - Spreading: Gravity and interfacial surface tension drive the oil to form a thin surface slick) Tj
T*
(   \(0.1 to 10 mm thickness\).) Tj
T*
(   - Evaporation: Low-molecular-weight volatile hydrocarbons \(C1 to C15, including toxic BTEX\)) Tj
T*
(   evaporate into the atmosphere within 24 to 48 hours \(accounting for up to 30-50% loss of total) Tj
T*
(   spill mass\).) Tj
T*
(   - Emulsification: Turbulent wave action drives water droplets into the viscous oil, forming a) Tj
T*
(   stable water-in-oil emulsion \('chocolate mousse'\) containing 60-80% water. This drastically) Tj
T*
(   increases viscosity and volume, impeding mechanical skimming.) Tj
T*
(   - Photo-oxidation & Dissolution: Solar UV radiation photo-oxidizes aromatics into polar) Tj
T*
(   carboxylic acids and ketones.) Tj
T*
(   2. Mechanical Containment and Physical Recovery:) Tj
T*
(   - Floating Containment Booms: Continuous floating barriers with an above-water freeboard and) Tj
T*
(   submerged skirt deployed to encircle and contain the spreading slick.) Tj
T*
(   - Oleophilic Skimmers: Rotating drum, disc, or mop skimmers coated with oleophilic polymers) Tj
T*
(   \(polypropylene\) that selectively adsorb hydrophobic crude oil while repelling water, followed) Tj
T*
(   by scraper blades that deposit recovered oil into storage tanks.) Tj
T*
(   3. In-Situ Bioremediation by Hydrocarbonoclastic Bacteria:) Tj
T*
(   - Following an oil spill, indigenous marine bacterial communities undergo dramatic population) Tj
T*
(   succession:) Tj
T*
