T*
(   2. Linear Energy Transfer \(LET\) and Relative Biological Effectiveness \(RBE\):) Tj
T*
(   - Linear Energy Transfer \(LET\): The average energy deposited per unit distance along the track) Tj
T*
(   of the ionizing particle:) Tj
T*
(   LET = -dE / dx [expressed in keV/micrometer].) Tj
T*
(   * Low-LET Radiation \(Gamma rays, X-rays, beta particles\): LET ~ 0.2 to 2 keV/um. Generates) Tj
T*
(   widely spaced, sparse ionization events.) Tj
T*
(   * High-LET Radiation \(Alpha particles, heavy recoiling nuclei\): LET ~ 100 to 200 keV/um.) Tj
T*
(   Generates dense, concentrated ionization tracks.) Tj
T*
(   - Relative Biological Effectiveness \(RBE\): The ratio of biological damage produced by a test) Tj
T*
(   radiation compared to reference 250 kVp X-rays. For alpha radiation, radiation weighting factor) Tj
T*
(   w_R = 20 \(meaning 1 Gray of alpha dose delivers 20 Sieverts of biological damage\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Molecular Radio-Pathology:) Tj
T*
(   - Water Radiolysis: Ionization of intracellular water generates high fluxes of reactive) Tj
T*
(   hydroxyl radicals:) Tj
T*
(   H2O + Radiation -> H2O+ + e- -> .OH + H+ + e_aq-.) Tj
T*
(   - Clustered DNA Lesions: While low-LET radiation induces simple repairable single-strand breaks) Tj
T*
(   \(SSBs\), high-LET alpha particles deposit localized energy clusters directly across the DNA) Tj
T*
(   double helix. This causes complex, clustered Double-Strand DNA Breaks \(DSBs\) where both) Tj
T*
(   complementary strands are cleaved within a few base pairs. Non-Homologous End Joining \(NHEJ\)) Tj
T*
(   repair fails, leading to chromosomal translocations, mitotic catastrophe, apoptosis, and) Tj
T*
(   leukemia.) Tj
