(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the reactor physics and environmental aftermath of the Chernobyl Nuclear Disaster \(1986\), detailing the Positive Void Coefficient.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Reactor Physics and Environmental Aftermath of the Chernobyl Nuclear Disaster \(1986\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Reactor Architecture: The RBMK-1000 Design:) Tj
T*
(   The Chernobyl Unit 4 reactor was a graphite-moderated, water-cooled thermal nuclear reactor) Tj
T*
(   \(RBMK-1000\) utilizing low-enriched uranium oxide fuel \(2% U-235\) with vertical pressure tubes:) Tj
T*
(   - Solid Graphite Moderator: Used to slow fast fission neutrons down to thermal energies.) Tj
T*
(   - Light Water Coolant: Liquid water circulated through pressure tubes to remove fission heat) Tj
T*
(   and generate steam.) Tj
T*
(   2. The Fatal Physics Flaw: The Positive Void Coefficient of Reactivity:) Tj
T*
(   - In most commercial nuclear reactors \(e.g., PWRs and BWRs\), liquid water acts as BOTH coolant) Tj
T*
(   and primary neutron moderator. If coolant boils into steam voids, neutron moderation ceases,) Tj
T*
(   shutting down the fission chain reaction \(Negative Void Coefficient, inherently fail-safe\).) Tj
T*
(   - In the RBMK reactor, graphite provides moderation, while liquid water acts primarily as a) Tj
T*
(   neutron ABSORBER \(parasitic poison\).) Tj
T*
(   - When cooling water boiled into steam \('voids'\), neutron absorption by liquid water plummeted,) Tj
T*
(   while graphite moderation continued unaffected.) Tj
T*
(   - This generated a lethal Positive Void Coefficient: More steam voids -> decreased neutron) Tj
T*
(   absorption -> increased core reactivity -> surging thermal fission power -> rapid localized) Tj
T*
(   boiling -> more steam voids in a runaway supercritical explosion!) Tj
T*
(   3. Control Rod Scram Design Flaw \(The Positive Scram Effect\):) Tj
T*
(   Boron carbide control rods featured 4.5-meter graphite displacement tips. When operators) Tj
T*
(   pressed the emergency scram button \(AZ-5\), the inserting graphite tips initially displaced) Tj
T*
(   neutron-absorbing water from the bottom of the core, causing a localized power spike \(exceeding) Tj
T*
(   30,000 MW_thermal, 10 times nominal full power\) that ruptured fuel channels.) Tj
T*
(   4. Explosive Detonation and Atmospheric Fallout:) Tj
T*
(   - Superheated steam explosion followed by a secondary hydrogen/air chemical explosion blew off) Tj
T*
