(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the sequence of events during the Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Disaster \(2011\), detailing Zircaloy-Water reactions and hydrogen explosions.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Disaster \(2011\): Station Blackout, Zircaloy Oxidation, and Hydrogen) Tj
T*
(   Explosions:) Tj
T*
(   1. Initiating Events: Earthquake and Tsunami \(March 11, 2011\):) Tj
T*
(   - The Great East Japan Earthquake \(magnitude 9.0\) triggered immediate automated emergency) Tj
T*
(   reactor scrams \(control rod insertion\) across Units 1, 2, and 3 at the Fukushima Daiichi) Tj
T*
(   Boiling Water Reactor \(BWR\) facility. Fission ceased, but decay heat continued at ~6-7% of full) Tj
T*
(   thermal power.) Tj
T*
(   - 45 minutes later, a 14-meter-high tsunami overtopped the 5.7-meter sea defense wall, flooding) Tj
T*
(   underground turbine basements and drowning all 12 emergency diesel generators and electrical) Tj
T*
(   switchgear.) Tj
T*
(   - This caused an instantaneous, total Station Blackout \(SBO\): Complete loss of all AC) Tj
T*
(   electrical power to run reactor core cooling pumps.) Tj
T*
(   2. Core Dewatering and Zircaloy-Water Hydrogen Generation:) Tj
T*
(   - When emergency steam-driven isolation condensers and turbine pumps depleted their battery) Tj
T*
(   reserves, reactor water boiled off, exposing uranium dioxide \(UO2\) fuel rods.) Tj
T*
(   - As bare fuel cladding temperatures surged above 1,200 deg C, the Zirconium alloy \(Zircaloy-4\)) Tj
T*
(   cladding underwent a rapid, highly exothermic chemical oxidation reaction with superheated) Tj
T*
(   steam:) Tj
T*
(   Zr \(s\) + 2 H2O \(g\) -> ZrO2 \(s\) + 2 H2 \(g\) + Delta H \(-586 kJ/mol\)) Tj
T*
(   - This reaction produced immense volumes of explosive molecular hydrogen \(H2\) gas while) Tj
T*
(   releasing chemical heat that accelerated fuel meltdown \(corium formation\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Primary Containment Over-Pressurization and Explosions:) Tj
T*
(   - Hydrogen and radioactive steam accumulated inside the primary containment vessel \(drywell\).) Tj
T*
(   To prevent drywell rupture, operators executed emergency venting into the secondary reactor) Tj
T*
(   service buildings.) Tj
T*
(   - Hydrogen accumulated beneath the flat roof of the reactor buildings. At a concentration of 4%) Tj
T*
(   in air, hydrogen ignited:) Tj
T*
(   * Unit 1: Devastating hydrogen deflagration destroyed the upper building structure on March 12.) Tj
T*
(   * Unit 3: Catastrophic hydrogen-air detonation shattered the building on March 14.) Tj
T*
(   4. Marine and Atmospheric Radiological Releases:) Tj
T*
(   - Major releases of volatile Iodine-131, Cesium-134, and Cesium-137 entered the atmosphere,) Tj
T*
(   carried east over the Pacific Ocean.) Tj
T*
(   - Millions of liters of highly contaminated cooling water leaked into the coastal marine) Tj
T*
(   environment, requiring installation of an engineered underground frozen-soil 'ice wall' and the) Tj
T*
(   Advanced Liquid Processing System \(ALPS\) to remove 62 radionuclides \(excluding tritium, H-3\).) Tj
