(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Multi-Barrier Engineering Architecture for High-Level Radioactive Waste \(HLW\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Radiological Nature of High-Level Waste:) Tj
T*
(   Spent nuclear reactor fuel consists of unburned uranium \(95%\), transuranic actinides \(Pu-239,) Tj
T*
(   Np-237, Am-241 with half-lives exceeding tens of thousands of years\), and short-to-medium-lived) Tj
T*
(   fission products \(Cs-137, Sr-90, Tc-99, I-129\). These wastes emit intense thermal heat and) Tj
T*
(   lethal gamma radiation, requiring permanent geological isolation for > 100,000 years.) Tj
T*
(   2. Chemical Vitrification into Borosilicate Glass:) Tj
T*
(   - Liquid HLW nitric acid extract is concentrated by evaporation, calcined at 500-800 deg C into) Tj
T*
(   solid dry oxides, and mixed with borosilicate glass frit \(SiO2: 50-60%, B2O3: 15-20%, Na2O:) Tj
T*
(   10-15%\).) Tj
T*
(   - Melting: The mixture is melted inside an induction-heated ceramic melter at 1,150 deg C. The) Tj
T*
(   radioactive polyvalent metal ions \(actinides, lanthanides, transition metals\) become chemically) Tj
T*
(   incorporated into the random network covalent silicon-oxygen-boron structural backbone.) Tj
T*
(   - Properties of Vitrified Waste:) Tj
T*
(   * Exceptional chemical durability: Leaching rate in groundwater is less than 10^-7 g/cm2/day.) Tj
T*
(   * High thermal conductivity and thermal stability up to 500 deg C.) Tj
T*
(   * High radiation tolerance: Amorphous glass matrix accommodates radiation displacement damage) Tj
T*
(   without swelling or macroscopic cracking.) Tj
T*
(   3. Multi-Barrier Geological Isolation \(KBS-3 Paradigm\):) Tj
T*
(   Vitrified canisters are emplaced in a Deep Geological Repository \(DGR\) excavated 500 meters) Tj
T*
(   underground within stable crystalline rock:) Tj
T*
(   - Engineered Barrier 1 \(Vitrified Waste Matrix\): Chemically locks rad-ions in glass.) Tj
T*
(   - Engineered Barrier 2 \(Overpack Canister\): High-purity corrosion-resistant thick Copper \(50) Tj
T*
(   mm\) or Titanium shell with a cast-iron inner structural support sleeve designed to withstand 50) Tj
T*
(   MPa hydrostatic and lithostatic pressure without mechanical failure for 100,000 years.) Tj
T*
(   - Engineered Barrier 3 \(Compacted Sodium Bentonite Clay\): Annular space around canisters is) Tj
T*
(   packed with dense swelling montmorillonite clay. When hydrated by groundwater, bentonite swells) Tj
T*
(   tightly against the rock, providing extremely low hydraulic permeability \(< 10^-12 m/s\),) Tj
T*
(   plastic self-healing of fractures, and chemical sorption of migrating cations.) Tj
T*
(   - Natural Geological Barrier 4 \(Deep Host Bedrock\): 500 meters of tectonically stable) Tj
T*
(   crystalline granite or bedded salt formations with zero regional groundwater movement.) Tj
T*
