(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate the Integrated Solid Waste Management \(ISWM\) hierarchy, evaluating the 5Rs and municipal waste flowsheets.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Integrated Solid Waste Management \(ISWM\): Hierarchy, 5Rs, and Municipal Flowsheets:) Tj
T*
(   1. Conceptual Framework of ISWM:) Tj
T*
(   Integrated Solid Waste Management is a comprehensive, multidisciplinary approach that combines) Tj
T*
(   waste characterization, collection, source segregation, material recovery, biochemical/thermal) Tj
T*
(   processing, and engineered containment to optimize economic efficiency and environmental) Tj
T*
(   protection.) Tj
T*
(   2. The 5Rs Waste Management Hierarchy \(In Descending Order of Preference\):) Tj
T*
(   - 1. Refuse \(Prevention\): Proactively refusing single-use non-recyclable products, excessive) Tj
T*
(   packaging, and toxic chemicals at source before entry into the municipal economy.) Tj
T*
(   - 2. Reduce \(Minimization\): Redesigning industrial manufacturing processes, extending product) Tj
T*
(   lifespan, and promoting lightweighting to minimize waste generation rates.) Tj
T*
(   - 3. Reuse \(Direct Re-utilization\): Cleaning and refurbishing products \(glass bottles, shipping) Tj
T*
(   pallets, electronic hardware\) for repeated identical or secondary uses without undergoing) Tj
T*
(   chemical transformation.) Tj
T*
(   - 4. Recycle \(Material Recovery\): Mechanically processing source-segregated recyclable) Tj
T*
(   materials \(paper, metals, PET/HDPE plastics, glass\) back into raw secondary manufacturing) Tj
T*
