T*
(   Engineering Architecture of Modern Sanitary Landfills: Multi-Barrier Liners, Leachate, and Gas) Tj
T*
(   Management:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Classification:) Tj
T*
(   A modern sanitary landfill is a containment facility engineered to isolate municipal solid) Tj
T*
(   waste from the surrounding environment \(subsoil, groundwater, atmosphere\) without creating) Tj
T*
(   environmental hazards or public health nuisances.) Tj
T*
(   2. Multi-Layer Composite Bottom Liner System \(Subtitle D / CPCB Standard\):) Tj
T*
(   Installed over a geotechnically compacted subgrade, progressing from bottom to top:) Tj
T*
(   - 1. Low-Permeability Compacted Clay Liner \(CCL\): A 60 to 90 cm thick layer of high-plasticity) Tj
T*
(   clay \(bentonite-amended soil\) compacted in 15-cm lifts to achieve a saturated hydraulic) Tj
T*
(   conductivity: K_sat <= 1.0 * 10^-7 cm/s \(10^-9 m/s\).) Tj
T*
(   - 2. Geomembrane Liner: A high-density polyethylene \(HDPE\) flexible membrane liner of minimum) Tj
T*
(   1.5 to 2.0 mm \(60-80 mil\) thickness, welded using double-track thermal fusion seams with) Tj
T*
(   continuous vacuum/pressure testing.) Tj
T*
(   - 3. Non-Woven Geotextile Cushion: A heavy needle-punched geotextile \(>= 400 g/m2\) placed) Tj
T*
(   directly over the HDPE sheet to prevent physical puncture by sharp gravel.) Tj
T*
(   - 4. Leachate Drainage Blanket: A 30 cm layer of washed round pea gravel \(permeability K >) Tj
T*
(   10^-2 cm/s\) graded to a 2% minimum slope toward collection sumps, embedding perforated HDPE) Tj
T*
(   collector pipes.) Tj
T*
(   3. Leachate Chemistry and Collection Hydraulics:) Tj
T*
(   - Leachate Composition: Extremely high COD \(10,000 to 60,000 mg/L in young landfills\), high) Tj
T*
(   ammonia-nitrogen \(1,000 to 3,000 mg/L\), volatile fatty acids, and heavy metals.) Tj
T*
(   - Submersible explosion-proof pumps in sump sumps maintain leachate head over the liner at < 30) Tj
T*
(   cm to prevent advective groundwater breakthrough.) Tj
T*
(   - Treatment: Multi-stage Biological Treatment \(Sequencing Batch Reactors, SBR\) combined with) Tj
T*
(   Advanced Oxidation \(Fenton\) and two-pass Reverse Osmosis \(RO\) with disk tube \(DTRO\) modules.) Tj
T*
(   4. Landfill Gas \(LFG\) Extraction and Energy Recovery:) Tj
T*
(   - Methanogenesis produces LFG consisting of 50-55% Methane \(CH4\) and 45-50% Carbon Dioxide) Tj
T*
(   \(CO2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Vertical perforated extraction wells \(100 to 200 mm diameter\) connected to an active vacuum) Tj
