(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the thermochemical combustion stages of Waste-to-Energy Incineration, flue gas scrubbing, and prevention of Dioxins and Furans \(PCDD/Fs\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Waste-to-Energy \(WtE\) Incineration: Thermal Kinetics, Flue Gas Cleaning, and PCDD/F) Tj
T*
(   Suppression:) Tj
T*
(   1. Thermochemical Combustion Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   Mass-burn moving-grate waste-to-energy incinerators process unsegregated municipal solid waste) Tj
T*
(   through three zones:) Tj
T*
(   - Drying & Pre-heating Zone: Refuse is heated to 100-200 deg C by radiant furnace heat and) Tj
T*
(   preheated under-grate air, driving off moisture.) Tj
T*
(   - Primary Combustion Zone: Solid waste undergoes pyrolysis, gasification, and solid carbon) Tj
T*
(   combustion on the grate at 800 to 950 deg C.) Tj
T*
(   - Secondary Combustion Chamber \(Afterburner\): Overfire secondary air is injected with high) Tj
T*
(   turbulence to completely oxidize volatile gaseous hydrocarbons and carbon monoxide at) Tj
T*
(   temperatures >= 850 deg C \(or >= 1,100 deg C for hazardous wastes\) for a minimum gas residence) Tj
T*
(   time of 2.0 seconds with >= 6% O2.) Tj
T*
(   2. Formation Mechanisms of Dioxins and Furans:) Tj
T*
(   Polychlorinated dibenzo-p-dioxins \(PCDDs\) and polychlorinated dibenzofurans \(PCDFs\) are) Tj
T*
(   extremely toxic, carcinogenic, and endocrine-disrupting planar aromatic compounds formed via) Tj
T*
(   two pathways:) Tj
T*
(   - High-temperature incomplete combustion of chlorinated plastics \(PVC\) and aromatic ring) Tj
T*
(   precursors \(chlorophenols\).) Tj
T*
(   - De-Novo Catalytic Synthesis in Post-Combustion Flue Gas: In the low-temperature flue gas) Tj
T*
(   cooling zone \(250 to 450 deg C\), unburned carbon soot reacts with gaseous HCl in the presence) Tj
T*
(   of transition metal catalysts \(copper chloride, CuCl2\) on fly ash surfaces to synthesize) Tj
T*
(   dioxins.) Tj
T*
(   3. Engineering PCDD/F Suppression Protocols:) Tj
T*
(   - The '3-T' Rule: Guarantee high Temperature \(> 850 deg C\), sufficient Time \(> 2.0 seconds\),) Tj
T*
(   and intense Turbulence to ensure complete destruction of organic precursors in the furnace.) Tj
T*
(   - Rapid Flue Gas Quenching: Passing boiler flue gas through an engineered spray dry) Tj
T*
(   evaporator/scrubber that drops temperature rapidly from 400 deg C down to < 180 deg C in less) Tj
T*
(   than 0.1 seconds, completely bypassing the de-novo synthesis temperature window!) Tj
T*
(   - Activated Carbon Injection \(ACI\): Finely powdered activated carbon \(PAC\) is continuously) Tj
T*
(   pneumatically injected into the flue gas duct upstream of the fabric filter baghouse. Porous) Tj
T*
(   PAC adsorbs vapor-phase dioxins, furans, and gaseous mercury, and is captured on the fabric) Tj
T*
(   filter bags.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
