(   * 1. Mesophilic Phase \(25 to 40 deg C, Days 1-3\): Fast-growing mesophilic bacteria \(Bacillus,) Tj
T*
(   Pseudomonas\) and fungi rapidly metabolize soluble, easily digestible sugars and amino acids,) Tj
T*
(   releasing heat.) Tj
T*
(   * 2. Thermophilic Phase \(50 to 65 deg C, Weeks 1-4\): As temperature rises, thermophilic) Tj
T*
(   spore-forming bacteria \(Thermus, Geobacillus\) and actinomycetes take over, degrading complex) Tj
T*
(   polymers \(starches, cellulose, hemicellulose\).) Tj
T*
(   Temperatures >= 55 deg C for at least 15 consecutive days are mandated to kill enteric) Tj
T*
(   viral/bacterial pathogens \(Salmonella, Shigella\) and weed seeds.) Tj
T*
(   * 3. Cooling and Maturation Phase \(40 to 25 deg C, Weeks 5-12\): Temperature declines. Fungi and) Tj
T*
(   actinomycetes synthesize polycondensed aromatic humic and fulvic acids, producing mature,) Tj
T*
(   earthy humus with C:N ratio < 15:1.) Tj
T*
(   2. Vermicomposting with Eisenia fetida \(Red Wiggler Earthworms\):) Tj
T*
(   - Epigeic Earthworm Physiology:) Tj
T*
(   Eisenia fetida is an epigeic litter-dwelling earthworm that does not burrow deep into mineral) Tj
T*
(   soils; it feeds voraciously on decaying organic matter at surface temperatures between 15 and) Tj
T*
(   25 deg C.) Tj
T*
(   - Gizzard Mastication and Gut Microbiome:) Tj
T*
(   * Earthworms lack teeth; food is mechanically ground with ingested mineral quartz particles) Tj
T*
(   inside the muscular gizzard.) Tj
T*
(   * The worm gut functions as a natural bioreactor rich in symbiotic digestive enzymes) Tj
T*
(   \(cellulases, chitinases, proteases\) and mucus.) Tj
T*
(   * Passage through the gut increases available nutrient concentrations \(available N, P, K\) by a) Tj
T*
(   factor of 3 to 10 compared to raw waste.) Tj
T*
(   - Vermicast Chemical Properties:) Tj
T*
(   Vermicompost excretions \(vermicasts\) are granulated, water-stable micro-aggregates rich in) Tj
T*
(   microbial plant-growth promoting hormones \(auxins, gibberellins, cytokinins\) and humic acids,) Tj
T*
(   exhibiting superior CEC and moisture-holding properties compared to thermal compost.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
