(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze thermochemical Pyrolysis and Gasification of Solid Wastes, comparing syngas production with direct incineration and plasma gasification.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Pyrolysis, Gasification, and Plasma Arc Technologies for Waste Valorization:) Tj
T*
(   1. Thermochemical Processing Regimes:) Tj
T*
(   - Incineration: Fully OXIDIZING regime \(Equivalence Ratio ER > 1.2 to 1.8, excess) Tj
T*
(   stoichiometric oxygen\). Complete combustion converts chemical energy into high-temperature flue) Tj
T*
(   gas \(CO2, H2O, N2\) to generate steam.) Tj
T*
(   - Gasification: PARTIALLY OXIDIZING regime \(Sub-stoichiometric oxygen: ER = 0.2 to 0.4\)) Tj
T*
(   operating at 800 to 1,200 deg C. Converts solid carbonaceous waste into synthesis gas \(Syngas,) Tj
T*
(   primarily CO, H2, and minor CH4\).) Tj
T*
(   - Pyrolysis: Strictly NON-OXIDIZING regime \(Zero oxygen: ER = 0\) conducted at 400 to 800 deg C.) Tj
T*
(   Thermally cracks complex organic polymers into three distinct product phases: Solid) Tj
T*
(   Biochar/Carbon Black, Liquid Pyrolysis Bio-Oil \(condensed condensable vapors\), and) Tj
T*
(   Non-condensable Syngas.) Tj
T*
(   2. Gasification Chemical Equilibrium Reactions:) Tj
T*
(   Inside a fluidized-bed gasifier, solid refuse-derived fuel \(RDF\) undergoes sequential) Tj
T*
(   endothermic and exothermic gasification reactions:) Tj
T*
(   - Heterogeneous Water-Gas Reaction: C \(s\) + H2O \(g\) <-> CO + H2 \(Delta H = +131 kJ/mol\)) Tj
T*
(   - Boudouard Reaction: C \(s\) + CO2 \(g\) <-> 2 CO \(Delta H = +172 kJ/mol\)) Tj
T*
(   - Homogeneous Water-Gas Shift \(WGS\): CO + H2O <-> CO2 + H2 \(Delta H = -41 kJ/mol\)) Tj
T*
(   - Methanation: C + 2 H2 <-> CH4 \(Delta H = -75 kJ/mol\).) Tj
T*
(   The resulting clean Syngas has a Lower Heating Value \(LHV\) of 4 to 12 MJ/Nm3, suitable for) Tj
T*
(   direct firing in high-efficiency combined-cycle gas turbines \(CCGT\) or catalytic upgrading via) Tj
T*
ET

