(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the regulatory classification of Hazardous Waste under the US EPA and Indian Rules: Ignitability, Corrosivity, Reactivity, and Toxicity.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Hazardous Waste Characterization, TCLP Protocol, and Secured Landfill Design:) Tj
T*
(   1. Statutory Hazardous Waste Criteria \(US EPA RCRA and Indian Rules 2016\):) Tj
T*
(   Solid, liquid, or sludge wastes are designated as Hazardous Waste if they exhibit any one of) Tj
T*
(   four defined hazardous characteristics:) Tj
T*
(   - 1. Ignitability \(Code D001\):) Tj
T*
(   * Liquids with a flash point < 60 deg C \(140 deg F\) via closed-cup tester \(e.g., spent solvents) Tj
T*
(   like acetone, toluene, benzene\).) Tj
T*
(   * Non-liquids capable under standard temperature and pressure of causing fire through friction,) Tj
T*
(   absorption of moisture, or spontaneous chemical changes.) Tj
T*
(   - 2. Corrosivity \(Code D002\):) Tj
T*
(   * Aqueous waste with pH <= 2.0 \(strongly acidic\) or pH >= 12.5 \(strongly alkaline\).) Tj
T*
(   * Liquids capable of corroding standard SAE 1020 steel at a rate exceeding 6.35 mm per year at) Tj
T*
(   55 deg C.) Tj
T*
(   - 3. Reactivity \(Code D003\):) Tj
T*
(   * Unstable substances capable of undergoing violent chemical changes, violent reactions with) Tj
T*
(   water, or forming potentially explosive mixtures.) Tj
T*
(   * Cyanide- or sulfide-bearing wastes releasing toxic gases \(HCN, H2S\) when exposed to pH) Tj
T*
(   between 2.0 and 12.5.) Tj
T*
(   - 4. Toxicity \(Code D004\):) Tj
T*
(   * Evaluated using the Toxicity Characteristic Leaching Procedure \(TCLP, EPA Method 1311\).) Tj
T*
(   2. The Toxicity Characteristic Leaching Procedure \(TCLP\):) Tj
T*
(   - Designed to simulate the chemical leaching of heavy metals and organics that would occur if) Tj
T*
(   waste were co-disposed in an unlined municipal landfill containing acidic humic acids.) Tj
T*
(   - Waste is crushed to < 9.5 mm and extracted with an acetic acid buffer \(pH 2.88 or 4.93\) for) Tj
T*
(   18 +/- 2 hours in a rotary agitation vessel at 30 rpm.) Tj
T*
(   - The filtered leachate extract is analyzed via ICP-MS or GC-MS against regulatory thresholds:) Tj
T*
(   Arsenic \(5.0 mg/L\), Cadmium \(1.0 mg/L\), Lead \(5.0 mg/L\), Mercury \(0.2 mg/L\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Secured Hazardous Waste Landfill Design:) Tj
T*
(   Requires a Double Composite Liner system comprising two separate geomembranes \(primary and) Tj
T*
(   secondary HDPE\), two independent compacted clay layers \(each >= 90 cm with K < 10^-9 m/s\), and) Tj
T*
(   a secondary Leak Detection and Removal System \(LDRS\) between the liners to detect any primary) Tj
T*
(   liner breach.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
