(   1. Statutory Regulatory Scope:) Tj
T*
(   Enacted under the Environment \(Protection\) Act, 1986, the Bio-Medical Waste Management Rules) Tj
T*
(   apply to all healthcare facilities, veterinary hospitals, and medical research laboratories. A) Tj
T*
(   strict color-coded source-segregation architecture is legally mandated:) Tj
T*
(   2. The Fourfold Color-Coded Segregation Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - 1. Yellow Color-Coded Non-Chlorinated Bags / Containers:) Tj
T*
(   * Waste Stream: Human anatomical tissues, organs, amputated body parts, animal carcasses,) Tj
T*
(   soiled plaster casts, cotton gauze contaminated with blood/body fluids, expired cytotoxic) Tj
T*
(   pharmaceuticals, and microbiology cultures.) Tj
T*
(   * Treatment & Disposal: Incineration in double-chamber incinerators \(primary chamber >= 800 deg) Tj
T*
(   C, secondary >= 1050 deg C\), or deep burial in remote areas.) Tj
T*
(   - 2. Red Color-Coded Containers:) Tj
T*
(   * Waste Stream: Contaminated recyclable plastics: intravenous tubing, catheters, urine bags,) Tj
T*
(   disposable plastic syringes \(without needles\), vacutainer tubes.) Tj
T*
(   * Treatment: Thermal disinfection via Autoclaving or Hydroclaving, followed by mandatory) Tj
T*
(   mechanical shredding to mutilate items, and recycling through authorized recyclers.) Tj
T*
(   - 3. White Translucent, Puncture-Proof, Tamper-Proof Containers:) Tj
T*
(   * Waste Stream: Waste Sharps \(used hypodermic needles, needles with fixed syringes, scalpels,) Tj
T*
(   surgical blades, contaminated glass slides\).) Tj
T*
(   * Treatment: Autoclaving or Dry Heat Sterilization, followed by encapsulation in) Tj
T*
(   concrete-filled steel drums or melting.) Tj
T*
(   - 4. Blue Cardboard Boxes / Rigid Bins:) Tj
T*
(   * Waste Stream: Broken or intact contaminated glassware \(medicine vials, ampoules\) and metallic) Tj
T*
(   orthopedic implants.) Tj
T*
(   * Treatment: Disinfection by soaking in 1-2% Sodium Hypochlorite solution or autoclaving,) Tj
T*
(   followed by recycling.) Tj
T*
(   3. Engineering Autoclaving Standards:) Tj
T*
(   - Gravity flow autoclaves must operate at >= 121 deg C at 15 psi pressure for >= 60 minutes.) Tj
T*
(   - Vacuum autoclaves must operate at >= 134 deg C at 31 psi for >= 45 minutes to achieve) Tj
T*
(   complete destruction of Geobacillus stearothermophilus endospores \(spore log reduction >= 4\).) Tj
T*
