(   [Problem Statement]: Explain hydrometallurgical and bioleaching metallurgical extraction processes for recovering Gold, Silver, and Copper from Electronic Waste.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Hydrometallurgical and Bioleaching Technologies for Metal Recovery from E-Waste:) Tj
T*
(   1. E-Waste as a Rich Secondary Urban Ore:) Tj
T*
(   Printed Circuit Boards \(PCBs\) from discarded computers and smartphones represent exceptionally) Tj
T*
(   rich mineral deposits. A single metric ton of PC circuit boards contains up to 200 to 250 grams) Tj
T*
(   of Gold \(Au\), 1,000 grams of Silver \(Ag\), and 150 to 200 kg of Copper \(Cu\), exhibiting precious) Tj
T*
(   metal grades 20 to 50 times richer than primary geological mined ores!) Tj
T*
(   2. Hydrometallurgical Extraction Flowsheet:) Tj
T*
(   - Mechanical Pre-treatment: PCBs are dismantled \(removing hazardous capacitors and batteries\),) Tj
T*
(   crushed, and pulverized to fine powders \(< 1 mm\).) Tj
T*
(   - Base Metal Leaching: Selective leaching of copper, nickel, and zinc using dilute sulfuric) Tj
T*
(   acid \(2 M H2SO4\) with hydrogen peroxide \(H2O2\) oxidant:) Tj
T*
(   Cu \(s\) + H2SO4 + H2O2 -> CuSO4 \(aq\) + 2 H2O.) Tj
T*
(   Copper is recovered from the pregnant leach solution via solvent extraction and electrowinning) Tj
T*
(   \(SX-EW\) as 99.99% pure cathode sheets.) Tj
T*
(   - Cyanide-Free Precious Metal Leaching \(Thiosulfate or Thiourea\):) Tj
T*
(   Traditional toxic cyanidation is replaced with eco-friendly ammonium thiosulfate leaching) Tj
T*
(   catalyzed by cupric ions:) Tj
T*
(   4 Au + 8 S2O3^2- + O2 + 2 H2O --[Cu2+]--> 4 [Au\(S2O3\)2]^3- + 4 OH-.) Tj
T*
